  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "Judge these screens. The question is: **could a person complete the flow from\nthese screens alone?**\n\nRead the mockups in order, as a stranger would. Where the sequence stops making\nsense is a real finding, not a nitpick.\n\n## The component docs\n\n{{.inputs.component_docs}}\n\n## The mockups\n\n{{.inputs.mockups}}\n\n## The flows they have to carry\n\n{{.inputs.flows}}\n\n## The docs this phase reads\n\n{{.inputs.working_set}}\n\n**These are paths, not contents.** Open each one with `read_file` before you start. Read the\nfile as it is now — an earlier state in this phase may have edited it since the run began.\n\n{{.inputs.near_matches}}\n\n_Paths — open them with `read_file`._\n\n## Findings from the previous pass\n\n{{.inputs.prior_findings}}\n\n## What to check\n\n- **Flow steps with nowhere to happen**, and elements on a surface no step needs.\n- **Does the hierarchy match the job, or the data model?** What reads first\n  should be what the person came for, not the field that happens to be the\n  primary key.\n- **Is a new component genuinely a different thing?** Compare it to its nearest\n  catalog entry by *purpose*, not appearance. Two that differ only in padding and\n  label are one component with a prop, and the doc has to say why this is not\n  that.\n- **Do the empty and error states carry the person forward?** An empty state\n  reading \"no items\" has spent the most teachable moment in the interface saying\n  nothing.\n- **Does the copy say what the person needs, or what the system did?**\n- **States omitted because they seemed unlikely.** Unlikely is not the bar.\n  Impossible is, and it has to be argued.\n- **Would the mockups alone get someone through the flow?**\n- **Departures from `direction.md`** are an exception or an amendment.\n\n## What to produce\n\n`findings` (severity · claim · evidence · target_id), `max_severity`,\n`max_severity_rank`, and `target`:\n\n- `draft` — the form is right, the docs or the rendering are not.\n- `explore` — the form itself is wrong; re-open the five designs.\n- `upstream` — **a finding that names a flow step rather than a rendering.** That\n  is a UX defect, not a UI one. Set `upstream`, and the gate always sees it: a\n  person routes it back to phase 2 rather than this phase fixing it locally.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "claude-opus-5"
    },
